---
title: Zombie
servings: 1
tags: [cocktail, rum]
source: Classic cocktail, number 18 on Drinks International's 2026 bestselling classics; method written for this repository
---

In a #blender{}, put @lime juice{0.75%fl_oz}, @falernum{0.5%fl_oz}, @grapefruit juice{0.5%fl_oz}, @cinnamon syrup{0.25%fl_oz}, @grenadine{1%tsp}, @Angostura bitters{1%dash}, @absinthe{6%drops}, @gold rum{1.5%fl_oz}, @Jamaican rum{1.5%fl_oz} and @overproof rum{1%fl_oz}(151 Demerara). Add a cup of crushed ice and blend for ~{5%seconds}. Pour, ice and all, into a #tall glass{} and garnish with a @fresh mint{1%sprig}.

> After Don the Beachcomber's 1934 recipe. The grapefruit and cinnamon syrup are his "Don's Mix". Strong: one is plenty.
